    {
      "type": "done",
      "answer": "No, CUDA local memory is not always on-chip. According to the lecture, local memory is thread-private in scope, but it usually resides in device DRAM and passes through the L1 and L2 caches [S1].\n\nThis is further supported by the description of the memory hierarchy, which states that a memory access traverses SM-local storage, L2, and device DRAM, with L2 misses continuing to a memory controller [S2]. Therefore, local memory accesses typically go off-chip to DRAM, rather than being stored exclusively on-chip like registers or shared memory.\n\n**Source:**\n- Page 46 [S1]\n- Page 44 [S2]",
      "citations": [
        {
          "document_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402",
          "chunk_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402-p46-1",
          "page": 46,
          "text": "GPU Memory Hierarchy\n\nEvery CUDA Memory Space Maps to a Physical Resource\n\n\n\n\n\n▪ Local memory is thread-private in scope but usually resides in device DRAM and\n  passes through L1/L2.\n▪ Register and shared-memory allocations limit how many blocks and warps can\n  reside on an SM.\n\nMemory Wall     CPU Memory    GPU Memory    SOTA Memory     Advanced AI Computing and Systems        46",
          "preview_url": "/api/documents/ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402/pages/46/preview",
          "source": "S1"
        },
        {
          "document_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402",
          "chunk_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402-p44-1",
          "page": 44,
          "text": "GPU Memory Hierarchy\n\nA Memory Access Traverses SM-Local Storage, L2, and Device\nDRAM\n\n\n\n\n\n▪ A request reaches device-wide L2 through the on-chip interconnect. An L2 miss\n  continues to a memory controller.\n▪ All SMs share L2 and the DRAM partitions, implemented with GDDR devices or\n HBM channels.\n\nMemory Wall     CPU Memory    GPU Memory    SOTA Memory     Advanced AI Computing and Systems        44",
          "preview_url": "/api/documents/ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402/pages/44/preview",
          "source": "S2"
        }
      ],
